## Role 4: The AI Web Developer — Building Your Website

A professional online presence is non-negotiable in 2026. Your website is your storefront, your credibility signal, and often the first impression a potential customer will have of your business. Hiring a web developer to build a custom site can cost anywhere from $2,000 to $20,000. Hiring an agency can cost significantly more. AI website builders have made this investment unnecessary for most early-stage businesses.

**Wix** has invested heavily in AI, and its ADI (Artificial Design Intelligence) system is among the most sophisticated free tools available. You answer a series of questions about your business, and the AI generates a fully designed, mobile-responsive website with placeholder content tailored to your industry. The free plan includes hosting, though it displays Wix branding. For a professional domain, the paid plan starts at a modest monthly fee — but for testing and early-stage validation, the free tier is entirely sufficient.

**Hostinger's AI Website Builder** takes a similar approach but with a stronger emphasis on speed. You can have a functional site live in under 30 minutes, complete with AI-generated copy for your homepage, about page, and services section.

For entrepreneurs who want more design control without learning to code, **Framer** offers a free tier with AI-powered design tools that translate text descriptions into functional web components. You can describe a section of your website in plain language — "a hero section with a bold headline, a subheading, and a call-to-action button in a dark blue color scheme" — and the AI will generate it.

One often-overlooked aspect of website building is copywriting. Your site can look beautiful and still fail to convert visitors into customers if the words are wrong. Use **ChatGPT** or **Claude** to write your website copy before you start building. Provide the AI with your business description, your target customer, and the specific action you want visitors to take, then ask it to write each page. This ensures your site is built around compelling copy rather than retrofitted with it.

